1,50$ bibliographie
1,2$Pileus hygrophanous, pallescent on drying, with or without aeriferous (givré) covering. 
1,23$Pileus not hygrophanous, not or only slightly pallescent on drying; without aeriferous covering. 
2,0$Pileipellis with inftated elements (physalids, intercalary cystidia); smell of smelt. $C. phaeophthalma
2,3$Pileipellis without such elements; smell different. 
3,10$Pileus without aeriferous covering (except at extreme margin). 
3,4$Pileus with aeriferous covering (givré). 
4,0$Lamellae grey; spores very small (3.0-4.0 x 2.5-3.5 um) $C. ditopa 
4,5$Lamellae whitish to pale crearn; spores larger. 
5,6$Spore print pinkish cream; spores in exsiccates in tetrads. 
5,7$Spore print white to cream. (without pink tinge); spores in exsiccates predominantly single. 
6,0$Pileus large (20-95 mm); lamellae broadly adnate; smell herbaceous $C. phyllophila 
6,0$Pileus medium (12-47 mm); lamellae decurrent; smell of aniseed $C. albofragrans 
7,8$Lamellae very crowded; smell pungent, herbaceous-acidulous; in forests. 
7,9$Lamellae less crowded; smell sweetish or farinaceous; usually outside forests between grasses. 
8,0$Spores ellipsoid to oblong; terrestrial. . $C. candicans 
8,0$Spores subglobose to broadly ellipsoid; on wood. . $C. tnmcicola 
9,0$Smell farinaceous; stipe longer than diameter of pileus $C. augeana 
9,0$Smell sweetish or indistinct; stipe shorter than diameter of pileus $ C. rivulosa 
10,14$smell and taste not rancid-farinaceous
10,11$Smell and taste rancid-farinaceous. 
11,0$Spores small, subglobose (3.0-4.0 x 2.5-3.5 um). $ C. ditopa 
11,12$Spores larger (more than 4.5 um long), ellipsoid. 
12,0$Pileipellis an ixocutis with distinctly incrusting pigment; in dune grassland $C. barbularum 
12,13$Pileipellis a (gelatinised) cutis with minutely incrusting pigment; in forests, heathlands, etc. 
13,0$Lamellae broadly adnate, ochraceous with olivaceous tinge. . $C. foetens 
13,0$Lamellae decurrent, grey to grey-brown $C. vibecina 
14,15$Spores on average 4.5-5.5 x 3.0-3.5 um 
14,19$Spores on average 5.5-9.0 x 3.5-4.5 um. 
15,0$Spore print white $C. subcordispora 
15,16$Spore print crearn to orange cream. 
16,0$Spores acyanophilous, in exsiccates single; on wood. $C. subbulbipes 
16,17$Spores cyanophilous, in exsiccates in tetrads; on leaf and needle litter. 
17,0$Pileus not striate, with reddish or pinkish tinge. . $C. diatreta 
17,18$Pileus translucently striate, without pinkish or reddish tinges. 
18,0$Pileus unicolorous, pale isabella or cream. $ C. agrestis 
18,0$Pileus with yellow-brown to brown centre and paler outer part. $C. marginella 
19,0$Smell strong, of aniseed $C. fragrans 
19,20$smell different. 
20,0$Lamellae and pileus with bright pink tinges; smell oftomato leaves $  C. boughtonii
20,21$Lamellae without bright pink tinges; smell different. 
21,0$Pileipellis with incrusting pigment; pileus with subinvolute margin $C. metachroides 
21,22$Pileipellis without incrusting pigment; pileus with straight margin. 
22,0$Spore print cream; stipe unicolorous; on dung, ruderal places, etc $C. amarescens 
22,0$Spore print white; stipe towards base darkening to dark grey-brown; in forests. . $C. metachroa 
23,24$Spores lacrymoid, with confluent base: pileus infundibuliform. 
23,28$Spores not lacrymoid, with obtuse to acute base; pileus convex to depressed. 
24,0$Pileus large (to 160 mm); stipe stout (13-20 mm); spores subglobose $C. geotropa 
24,25$Pileus smaller (to 80 mm); stipe less stout (3-8 mm); spores ellipsoid to oblong. 
25,0$Stipe whitish; pileipellis in exsiccate not darkening in KOH $C. gibba 
25,26$Stipe concolorous with pileus, isabella, brown or reddish brown; pileipellis dark brown with KOH. 
26,0$Pileus red to red-brown $C. glareosa 
26,27$Pileus isabella to greyish brown. 
27,0$Pileipellis a cutis; margin ofpileus often costate $C. costata 
27,0$Pileipellis a trichoderm, especially in the centre; pileus squamulose, at margin never costate.$ C. squamulosa 
28,0$smell strong, of aniseed $C. odora 
28,29$Smell not of aniseed. 
29,0$Spore print deep ochraceous; lamellae very crowded $ C. nebularis 
29,30$Spore print white to pale cream; lamellae crowded to subdistant. 
30,31$Stipe with conspicuous rhizoids. 
30,32$Stipe without conspicuous rhizoids. 
